{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence","id":1454756,"title":"Through the Ages - what events would you like to be at or influence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-12T11:24:22-07:00","id":1454756,"title":"Through the Ages - what events would you like to be at or influence","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> We are playing a through the ages campaign and are at the moment in ancient Sumeria (3500 BC). Thus far the campaign has been a blast even though it feels at times like a fun history lesson <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> To put it in perspective, writing (cuneiform) is going to be a new thing between now and a couple of hundred years. There are very few to no other vampires and even other supernaturals are rare. According to what we understood, in our reality the second city kinda just fell or is about to fall.<br /> <br /> Since we are in Sumer, we thought to join the siege of Mashkan-Shapir but after that, we are kinda.. stomped? Are there events in the World of Darkness where we should try to be at, try to influence one way or the other? Even if they are in the &quot;future&quot;, it gives something to work towards.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T11:31:36-07:00","id":1454758,"title":"","content":"Julian the <i>Apostate - </i>make his campaign successful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T12:45:40-07:00","id":1454764,"title":"","content":"There's so much history to pick from, it's hard to know where to go.<br /> Well, I'm currently filling in the blanks between steps in campaigns going through ancient history into the Modern Nights .<br /> <br /> Starting with Rome, the events currently standing out to me are the Punic Wars and whatever was going on with Carthage, the various expansions of the Roman Empire, the Eternal Senate setting the blueprints of the Camarilla and then the events surrounding the Great Fire of Rome and exploring the various tensions of Nero's reign (I'm going to see if I can get a player to cause the fire. A great story for the grandchilder... if they survive the fire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 07-12-2021, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T07:33:33-07:00","id":1455373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1454764#post1454764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's so much history to pick from, it's hard to know where to go.<br /> Well, I'm currently filling in the blanks between steps in campaigns going through ancient history into the Modern Nights .<br /> <br /> Starting with Rome, the events currently standing out to me are the Punic Wars and whatever was going on with Carthage, the various expansions of the Roman Empire, the Eternal Senate setting the blueprints of the Camarilla and then the events surrounding the Great Fire of Rome and exploring the various tensions of Nero's reign (I'm going to see if I can get a player to cause the fire. A great story for the grandchilder... if they survive the fire).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I totally get that. We are now 3500 BC. Script is still not a thing for a few hundred years and Rome or even Ancient Greece is 2000+ years in the future. So the ST has a lot of ground to cover but like I said, it's a history lesson.<br /> <br /> We are also looking forward to the Punic wars and are still in doubt who we want to help or assist.<br /> <br /> Other moments we are looking forward to, even if not for the event itself:<ul><li>The Labyrinth of Knosos</li> <li>Cursing of Clan Assamite (we have an Assamite Warrior in the party)</li> <li>Anarchy in Europe (diablerie galore and rise up against the elders)</li> <li>Convention of Thorns</li> <li>Sabbat vs Camarilla (still in doubt if we want to join either at that point)</li> <li>Creation of Clan Tremere and of Clan Giovanni</li> </ul>From a purely Historical point of View:<ul><li>Egypt versus Minoan civilization (where to go?)</li> <li>Ancient Greece, establishing of the City States</li> <li>Rome (of course)</li> <li>Punic Wars</li> <li>We are in doubt between going to Germany or France after this. Both have appeal</li> <li>And then of course the rest of history.</li> </ul><br /> It is kinda hard to find very interesting things before 2000 BCE<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T07:34:07-07:00","id":1455374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1454758#post1454758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Julian the <i>Apostate - </i>make his campaign successful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine this is a pun I am totally missing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T08:22:00-07:00","id":1455381,"title":"","content":"Julian the Apostate was a Roman emperor who wanted the empire to return to its pagans roots when it was becoming Christian. He died before he could accomplish anything significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T09:39:07-07:00","id":1455389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1455381#post1455381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Julian the Apostate was a Roman emperor who wanted the empire to return to its pagans roots when it was becoming Christian. He died before he could accomplish anything significant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So yes, I was totally looking at this from a White Wolf point of view thinking about Baali and whatever not. But it was just plain and simple, very embarassing... History. Thanks for the reminder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T16:02:17-07:00","id":1455401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1455373#post1455373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are now 3500 BC.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1455373#post1455373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is kinda hard to find very interesting things before 2000 BCE</div> </div> </div> </div>What things your group finds interesting is certainly a matter of personal taste. But here are some things that will occur between 3500 and 2000 BC which you may be able to use if you want to continue playing during this time.<br /> <br /> The horse is domesticated on the Eurasian steppe around 3500. So probably within a few hundred years of that, Sumeria will see the introduction of the domesticated horse for the first time. But it will basically be a beast of burden. Chariot warfare will not appear until about the 18th/17th centuries.<br /> <br /> The first recorded war in history beguns circa 2700 BC between Sumer and Elam.<br /> <br /> The likely historical King Gilgamesh reigns around 2600 BC. There is a lot of WoD lore around this figure in both Vampire and Werewolf (and maybe Mage, I'm not sure). You can probably pillage a lot of lore to figure out something to do.<br /> <br /> Sargon the Conqueror creates the first empire in history, the Akkadian, around 2300 BC.<br /> <br /> The Early Dynastic and Old Kingdom periods of Egypt exists during this time (3100-2700 and 2700-2200 BC respectively). The first Pyramids are built during this time. It's rise and fall might be interesting. A lot of WoD lore exists of this time, particularly in regards to Set's war with... pretty much everyone. But he won't be defeated until around 1750 BC. Honestly, someone really interested in Egyptology could probably run an entire chronicle set during this time alone. There's just enough historical information to give you direction, but not too much to bog you down in details (in one of my books on Ancient Egypt history this is only about 70 pages). And there's so much we don't know and controversies on chronology, that you can put in a lot that you want while still acknowledging the points of history you want.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T03:09:05-07:00","id":1455427,"title":"","content":"If you just want a fun history romp, what you're doing is cool, but if you want a more -serious- history game, I'd advise against it. <br /> <br /> A lot of history is interesting, but not all of it is famous, especially as to how people tend to learn history in school as it supposedly relates to them. Going for something lesser-known but still interesting would really help you avoid looking like a -greatest hits- collection that lacks context. Your vampires don't know who's going to be the next big thing in all likelyhood. Folks like Alexander the Great or Ghenghis Khan really jump out of the woodwork (Mongols were predictable, but Ghenghis really took them a few extra miles with reforms) and there's a lot of misleading information. For example, Hungary of all places was at some point the richest place in europe, lithuania at one point was the largest; look at them now. History is predictable, but there's too much unexpected. That, and, well, you have to move around to mess with all the &quot;big&quot; events and vampires really don't like moving around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T10:53:20-07:00","id":1455450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1455401#post1455401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> What things your group finds interesting is certainly a matter of personal taste. But here are some things that will occur between 3500 and 2000 BC which you may be able to use if you want to continue playing during this time.<br /> <br /> The horse is domesticated on the Eurasian steppe around 3500. So probably within a few hundred years of that, Sumeria will see the introduction of the domesticated horse for the first time. But it will basically be a beast of burden. Chariot warfare will not appear until about the 18th/17th centuries.<br /> <br /> The first recorded war in history beguns circa 2700 BC between Sumer and Elam.<br /> <br /> The likely historical King Gilgamesh reigns around 2600 BC. There is a lot of WoD lore around this figure in both Vampire and Werewolf (and maybe Mage, I'm not sure). You can probably pillage a lot of lore to figure out something to do.<br /> <br /> Sargon the Conqueror creates the first empire in history, the Akkadian, around 2300 BC.<br /> <br /> The Early Dynastic and Old Kingdom periods of Egypt exists during this time (3100-2700 and 2700-2200 BC respectively). The first Pyramids are built during this time. It's rise and fall might be interesting. A lot of WoD lore exists of this time, particularly in regards to Set's war with... pretty much everyone. But he won't be defeated until around 1750 BC. Honestly, someone really interested in Egyptology could probably run an entire chronicle set during this time alone. There's just enough historical information to give you direction, but not too much to bog you down in details (in one of my books on Ancient Egypt history this is only about 70 pages). And there's so much we don't know and controversies on chronology, that you can put in a lot that you want while still acknowledging the points of history you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Our Storyteller is an a history major so I am expecting unexpected and great things from him. He has come up with maps of places we didn't even knew existed and kept us busy there for hours on end trying to figure out what something was and how it worked. That is for me one of the most attractive points in this campaign, that we are kinda discovering great things about human history and learning while playing. It's not even textbook boring, so that is a plus.<br /> <br /> Egypt we'll try to avoid I think since it's so overdone and I presume we are going to go the menoan side of things since that is more &quot;open&quot; and we kinda don't wanna be in the middle of the setite thing. I imagine that is a preference but again, it's his choice ultimately and we'll gladly move along.<br /> <br /> So it's going to be a blast either way but thanks for the tips <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T10:56:34-07:00","id":1455451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1455427#post1455427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just want a fun history romp, what you're doing is cool, but if you want a more -serious- history game, I'd advise against it.<br /> <br /> A lot of history is interesting, but not all of it is famous, especially as to how people tend to learn history in school as it supposedly relates to them. Going for something lesser-known but still interesting would really help you avoid looking like a -greatest hits- collection that lacks context. Your vampires don't know who's going to be the next big thing in all likelyhood. Folks like Alexander the Great or Ghenghis Khan really jump out of the woodwork (Mongols were predictable, but Ghenghis really took them a few extra miles with reforms) and there's a lot of misleading information. For example, Hungary of all places was at some point the richest place in europe, lithuania at one point was the largest; look at them now. History is predictable, but there's too much unexpected. That, and, well, you have to move around to mess with all the &quot;big&quot; events and vampires really don't like moving around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think we are going to move around that much.<br /> <br /> How I think it's going to go (and I could be very wrong as I've already been wrong multiple times in this campaign) we are going to go Minoan, Mycean, Rome and from there up in Europe. Might also be Egyptian, Carthaginian (sp?), Rome (?), Europe or some such.<br /> <br /> So I don't think we'll see a lot of Genghis Khan except him ehm.. raiding and destroying things we are trying to build up. I really don't know a lot about eastern europe history so it would be great to find out a lot more about that. But like I said, we'll have a blast playing through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T20:07:35-07:00","id":1455553,"title":"","content":"The Bronze Age collapse.<br /> <br /> Alexander the Great's empire and its immediate aftermath, including the successor kingdoms in Egypt and western India. <br /> <br /> The third century crisis in the Roman Empire. <br /> <br /> The reign of Charlemagne.<br /> <br /> The Norman invasions of England (including Mithras awakening and eventually coming to power)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T11:48:16-07:00","id":1455672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454756-through-the-ages-what-events-would-you-like-to-be-at-or-influence?p=1455553#post1455553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bronze Age collapse.<br /> <br /> Alexander the Great's empire and its immediate aftermath, including the successor kingdoms in Egypt and western India.<br /> <br /> The third century crisis in the Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> The reign of Charlemagne.<br /> <br /> The Norman invasions of England (including Mithras awakening and eventually coming to power)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2-5 I can relate to as they are all pivotal or very specific historical moments. <br /> Why would you want to be present at the bronze age collapse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}